{"question_id": "V2-dev-RPT-en-T2-002", "approach": "LEX5", "approach_base": "LEX5", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "D", "corpus_set": "D_en", "answer_text": "Delivery Hero treats the pre-August 2021 Spanish rider risk as probable, recognizing provisions, while the post-August 2021 model risk is treated as possible and disclosed only as a contingency.\n\n- For the model operated by Glovo until August 2021, where it is more likely than not that the risk materializes, appropriate provisions are reflected in the Consolidated Financial Statements [1].\n- For Glovo Spain after August 2021, the risk is deemed possible but not probable, so it is disclosed as a contingency [1]; the auditor's report notes a contingent liability of €440 to 770 million for the investigation concerning the model operated since August 2021 [2].\n- Glovo decided to progressively move to an employment-based model in Spain (announced December 2024, effective 2025) to avoid further legal uncertainties regarding the model in place since August 2021 [3][4][6].\n- For the pre-August 2021 proceedings, Glovo had to provide bank guarantees to Spanish courts in 2024 to secure claimed liabilities, and it will defend the self-employed status through all available instances while cooperating with authorities [3][5].", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 1029 chars]", "doc_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en", "section_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::h201", "unit_ids": ["D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::p128_b3", "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::p128_b9"], "kind": "package", "score": null, "rank": null, "span": [465758, 466787], "meta": {"chunk": 17005, "completed": 104, "prefix": 0}}, {"text": "[stripped: 720 chars]", "doc_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en", "section_id": "D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::h355", "unit_ids": ["D.deliveryhero_annual-report_2024.en::p225_b5", "D.deliveryhero_annual-re